&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team/ Role Paragraph:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coinbase is building the future of institutional trading as part of the Everything Exchange, powering the systems that let the world&#39;s largest financial institutions trade across markets with speed, depth, and trust. As an Architect on the Trading team, you&#39;ll design, build, and own the core trading systems that power Coinbase: order and execution management, algo execution, settlement, multi-venue connectivity, and low-latency messaging that serve our Retail, Prime, and wholesale brokerage customers. It&#39;s a rare chance to architect trading infrastructure from the ground up, with the ownership of a startup and the reach of Coinbase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture of the end-to-end trading platform: the sequencer, the low-latency connectivity and messaging fabric, OMS/EMS, multi-venue connectivity, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design low-latency, high-throughput systems for real-time financial products used across institutional and retail markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive reliability and performance, owning SLOs, observability, and incident response for systems where correctness and latency are non-negotiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical bar through code, design reviews, and standards, and pay down the technical debt that matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce single-point-of-failure risk across the trading stack and build team resilience through mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product, Risk, Security, and Compliance to turn technical vision into a roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on architect, able to design, build, deploy, and support 24/7 trading systems that process billions of dollars of transactions daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive backend engineering experience, with demonstrated ownership of complex, production-grade distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of architecting an end-to-end trading platform (OMS, front/middle office, multi-exchange connectivity), not just a single gateway.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in low-latency Java and high-throughput messaging (Aeron, SBE, or similar), designing event-driven, high-availability systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering projects end-to-end: scoping, architecture, implementation, monitoring, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building systems in a regulated or financial environment where correctness, auditability, and low-latency performance are critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making user-facing product decisions that balance engineering trade-offs with end-user quality, demonstrated through shipped products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible use of generative AI, with human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Position ID: &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;P77879&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
