&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Backend leaning Software Engineer. In this role, you will be pivotal in designing, building, and maintaining scalable, high-performance systems. Leveraging JavaScript/TypeScript, Node.js, SQL and NoSQL cloud-native databases, and AWS, you will develop innovative solutions for user, group, and membership management while ensuring the highest levels of security and reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday. If you&#39;re located beyond that distance, the role is fully remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable us to deliver secure, reliable, and scalable services that exceed industry standards and customer expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver large-scale projects with cross-team dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with peer teams to deliver solutions that meet industry standards and customer expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and operate services at high scale, participating in scheduled on-call rotations to ensure reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement identity synchronization and lifecycle management solutions using SCIM and other relevant standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Kubernetes, etc.) to deliver scalable, high-availability applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain high-quality enterprise software using TypeScript, REST APIs, and JSON.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in TypeScript/JavaScript, React, and Node.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of security architecture, LDAP, Active Directory, SAML, SSO, OAuth2, OpenID Connect and web protocols like XML, SOAP, JSON, and REST.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with access control models such as RBAC, ABAC and ReBAC.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience developing and improving applications written in Node.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit excellent problem-solving abilities and effective communication skills, especially when collaborating with diverse teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Compensation:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $196,000-$294,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-CL1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for more information on how we handle your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our mission at Duolingo is to develop the best education in the world and make it universally available. It’s a big mission, and that’s where you come in!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Duolingo, you’ll join a team that cares about educating our users, experimenting with big ideas, making fact-based decisions, and finding innovative solutions to complex problems. You’ll have limitless learning opportunities and daily collaborations with world-class minds — while doing work that’s both meaningful and fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our life-changing mission to develop education for our half a billion (and growing!) learners around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.duolingo.com/?utm_source=greenhouse.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=generalblog_gh_091224&quot;&gt;our blog&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to build Duolingo Ads, Duolingo’s direct ad business. Most learners use our free, ad‑supported app—so great ads are core to our mission. We’re hiring a Head of West Coast Sales to open and scale our West Coast region. You will set regional strategy, build and lead a high‑performing team, and own revenue outcomes across priority verticals and agency holding companies. As a player/coach, you’ll cultivate senior‑level relationships, shape pricing and packaging with leadership, and close high‑impact deals that both delight learners and drive revenue while leading a team of sellers. This is a high‑ownership, early‑stage opportunity to help define how ads show up for hundreds of millions of learners while building a repeatable, data‑driven go‑to‑market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧠&amp;nbsp; You will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own West Coast revenue targets and forecasting; build a healthy, predictable pipeline across named accounts and agency groups, and deliver against quarterly goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the regional go‑to‑market strategy, including territory design, vertical focus, pricing/packaging inputs, and coverage plans as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and lead a small team of sellers over time; establish operating rhythms, deal reviews, and CRM hygiene standards that improve forecast accuracy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deepen senior relationships at brands and agencies; open new logos and expand strategic accounts with clear commercial narratives that map Duolingo’s unique strengths (design, IP, native formats) to client objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex deals end‑to‑end—from prospecting and positioning through negotiation, close, renewal, and expansion—partnering tightly with Account Management and Ad Ops for flawless delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share actionable market feedback with sales and product leadership to inform pricing, packaging, measurement, and ad experiences while protecting the learner experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with speed and rigor in a startup‑like environment, building repeatable sales motions, outreach cadences, and team practices that scale from 0→1 and 1→N.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✅&amp;nbsp; You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of direct digital ad sales experience with a consistent track record of hunting, closing, and renewing in premium mobile or consumer app environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Success selling video and native/custom formats and structuring innovative agreements with top‑tier advertisers and agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to engage senior decision makers while rolling up your sleeves to build collateral, troubleshoot issues, and drive revenue personally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ad tech and mobile app ecosystems, with skill using data to assess performance and inform pricing and packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, and comfort operating with ambiguity at high velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐&amp;nbsp; Exceptional candidates will have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships across West Coast brand and agency decision makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience introducing or scaling a new ads product from 0→1 within a publisher or platform environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping regional GTM, sales process, or coverage models beyond an individual book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity partnering with Account Management and Ad Ops on native/custom programs and live‑campaign storytelling to drive renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vertical expertise in Entertainment, Gaming, Streaming, or Tech that accelerates early traction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The offered salary is dependent upon several factors, including work experience, skills, and internal peer comparisons. The posted range is subject to change in the future. For this role, base salary is supplemented by equity compensation. We encourage you to talk with your recruiter for more information related to compensation for this role!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range: &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$228,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;Z7ph2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Take a peek at how we care for our employees&#39; holistic well-being with our benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.duolingo.com/#benefits&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Alerts:&lt;/strong&gt; Sign up for job alerts &lt;a href=&quot;http://my.greenhouse.io/users/sign_in?job_board=duolingo&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations: &lt;/strong&gt;We will do everything we can within reason to make sure that your interview takes place in an environment that fairly and accurately assesses your skills. If you need assistance or accommodation, please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@duolingo.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@duolingo.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity: &lt;/strong&gt;Duolingo is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraud Warning: &lt;/strong&gt;Unfortunately, there is a rise in scammers pretending to be real Duolingo employees. Duolingo and our employees will never ask for your Social Security number, bank details, or passport info, and we’ll never ask you to deposit a check, purchase equipment, or exchange money during the interview process. Real Duolingo employees always use an email that ends in @duolingo.com or @recruiting.duolingo.com. Stay alert and double-check these details before sharing any information.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;By applying for this position your data will be processed as per the&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vTX9GKeRMOMA9Vtm0vfGibrYPYz8ysl0Dg8KSXgj_PxeT5ChsdnNZZWtpxu4t7xillTPGnngnKCjIbV/pub&quot;&gt; Duolingo Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Proactive Threat team is responsible for identifying vulnerabilities and security weaknesses across Stripe&#39;s systems, applications, networks, and cloud infrastructure — before adversaries do. We operate as a hybrid offensive function: conducting penetration testing, emulating real-world threat actors through red team operations, and partnering closely with our defensive security teams to validate detection capabilities and improve Stripe&#39;s overall security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are builders first. Our team develops custom tooling, automation frameworks, and internal platforms that scale our offensive capabilities and enable repeatable, high-fidelity assessments. We believe the best offensive security engineers are equal parts hacker and engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is distributed across the United States, primarily operating in Eastern and Pacific time zones, and collaborates regularly with security, engineering, and product stakeholders across Stripe — including teams in Europe and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Offensive Security Engineer on the Proactive Threat team, you will simulate the tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) of real-world adversaries to uncover security risks across Stripe&#39;s products and infrastructure. You&#39;ll conduct hands-on penetration testing, lead red team engagements, and collaborate with blue team counterparts to validate and improve detection and response capabilities. Your work will directly influence how Stripe builds, ships, and secures financial infrastructure used by millions of businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond assessments, you&#39;ll design and build offensive tooling and automation that amplifies the team&#39;s impact. You&#39;ll leverage threat intelligence to prioritize testing efforts, contribute to incident investigations when needed, and act as a subject-matter expert for security initiatives across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct comprehensive penetration tests across web applications, APIs, cloud environments (AWS/GCP/Azure), mobile applications, and internal infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute red team engagements that emulate the TTPs of cyber and criminal threat actors targeting financial services, including initial access, lateral movement, persistence, and data exfiltration scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform assumed-breach and objective-based assessments to test detection and response capabilities in coordination with defensive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with detection engineering, threat intelligence, and incident response teams to validate security controls, identify coverage gaps, and improve detection fidelity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute adversary tradecraft insights to inform detection rule development, threat hunting hypotheses, and incident response playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support incident investigations by providing offensive expertise, log analysis, and root cause analysis when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain custom offensive tools, scripts, and automation frameworks to enhance assessment efficiency and coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal platforms and workflows that enable scalable, repeatable offensive operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal security tooling repositories and champion engineering best practices within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate repetitive testing tasks, payload generation, and reporting workflows using modern development practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear, actionable reports that communicate technical findings, business risk, and remediation guidance to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject-matter expert and primary point of contact for stakeholder teams engaged in offensive security programs and Stripe-wide security initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead offensive security projects end-to-end, mentor junior team members, and foster a culture of continuous learning and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and attack techniques; share research internally and contribute to the broader security community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in offensive security, penetration testing, red teaming, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages, with demonstrated experience building tools, automation, or custom exploits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of web application security, including OWASP Top 10, ASVS, and common vulnerability classes (injection, auth flaws, business logic, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP), including cloud-native attack techniques and misconfigurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with offensive tooling such as Burp Suite, Cobalt Strike, Mythic, Sliver, BloodHound, or similar frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with adversary tradecraft and frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, including TTPs for initial access, privilege escalation, lateral movement, and exfiltration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex technical findings into clear, risk-based recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think like an adversary — creative, persistent, and able to holistically assess risk in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting offensive security in fintech, financial services, or other highly regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in vulnerability research, exploit development, or CVE discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with threat intelligence, detection engineering, or incident response teams (purple team operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with big data and log analysis tools (Splunk, Databricks, PySpark, osquery, etc.) for threat hunting or investigative support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI/LLM-assisted development tools (e.g., Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot) and experience applying them to offensive security workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest or experience in agentic automation — using LLMs or autonomous agents to augment reconnaissance, vulnerability discovery, or exploitation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing AI/ML systems or LLM-based applications for security weaknesses (prompt injection, training data extraction, model manipulation, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source security tools, published research, blog posts, or conference presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as OSCP, OSWE, OSEP, OSED, CRTO, CPTS, PNPT, GXPN, or cloud security certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is remote within the United States. While you are welcome to visit Stripe offices for team meetings, on-sites, and events, our expectation is that you would regularly work from home. The team primarily coordinates across Eastern and Pacific time zones, with regular collaboration with stakeholders in Europe and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual US base salary range for this role is $170,400 – $255,700. This range may span multiple career levels and will be refined during the interview process based on experience, qualifications, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity participation in Stripe&#39;s growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with matching contributions from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness stipends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual budget for training, certifications, and conference attendance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Gusto&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Gusto, we&#39;re on a mission to grow the small business economy. We handle the hard stuff — payroll, health insurance, 401(k)s, and HR — so owners can focus on their craft and their customers. With teams in Denver, San Francisco, and New York, we support more than 500,000 small businesses nationwide and are building a workplace that reflects the people we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All full-time employees receive competitive base pay, benefits, and equity (RSUs) — because everyone who helps build Gusto should share in its success. Offer amounts are determined by role, level, and location. Learn more about our&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/total-rewards&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt; &lt;u&gt;Total Rewards philosophy&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is a fundamental part of how work gets done at Gusto. We expect all team members to actively engage with AI tools relevant to their role and grow their fluency as the technology evolves. AI experience requirements vary by role and will be assessed during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your chance to own one of the most technical, horizontal levers in GTM planning: building the scalable models and infrastructure that enable every route to market to grow efficiently. As Senior Sales Operations Analyst, you’ll partner with GTM leaders, Finance, Revenue Operations, and GTM Ops to develop and execute segmentation, book-of-business design, quota setting, and capacity planning. You’ll turn GTM strategy into concrete, automated models that determine how customers are segmented, how reps are staffed, and what they are held accountable for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role takes an end-to-end, platform-minded view across GTM motions, not just a single sales team. You’ll identify where manual work, fragmented logic, or inconsistent processes limit scale and build durable planning infrastructure that drives revenue outcomes as the business evolves. You’ll own the outcome: balanced books, defensible quotas tied to capacity, and scalable models that hold up under scrutiny.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll sit within GTM Operations, working as the dedicated segmentation, book-of-business, and capacity planning owner for our Direct, Expansion, and Benefits sales teams. We think of ourselves as builders and problem solvers: we turn ambiguous planning questions into scalable, defensible models, and we hold the line on rigor even when the business is moving fast and priorities compete.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work in close partnership with each organization&#39;s GTM leaders and their dedicated GTM Ops partners, leaning on their operational and business context, while you own building, defending, and maintaining the segmentation, book, quota, and headcount models that everyone plans against.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll do day-to-day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Segmentation &amp;amp; Book of Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design and ongoing maintenance of customer/account segmentation for Direct, Expansion, and Benefits sales, translating org-level segmentation strategy into concrete, rules-based models these teams can operate against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain balanced books of business across reps and teams, accounting for account potential, workload, geography, and product mix; own rebalancing when the business shifts (new hires, departures, territory changes, book splits).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and maintain clear, documented rules for account assignment, routing, and reclassification, and serve as the ruling authority when edge cases or disputes come up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, GTM Ops, and Systems &amp;amp; Tooling to ensure segmentation and book structures are reflected accurately in Salesforce and downstream systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quota Setting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end quota-setting process for Direct, Expansion, and Benefits: translating top-down revenue targets into bottoms-up, capacity-based quotas by rep, team, and segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the quota models and methodology, ensuring quotas are defensible, equitable across territories/books, and tightly tied to book-of-business design and headcount capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with RTM leaders, Finance, and Sales Compensation to align quotas with comp plans, revenue targets, and business priorities each planning cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quota administration through the cycle: true-ups for territory or book changes, new-hire ramp adjustments, and mid-cycle corrections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Headcount &amp;amp; Capacity Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM Ops &amp;amp; Finance on capacity planning for Direct, Expansion, and Benefits: modeling the headcount needed to cover segmented books and hit revenue targets, and identifying where the org is over- or under-staffed relative to opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the headcount models that inform hiring plans, partnering with RTM leaders and Finance on timing, sequencing, and prioritization of new roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously monitor capacity against actual book size, productivity, and attrition, flagging gaps or imbalances before they become a problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own scenario planning for headcount and territory changes (reorgs, new segments, M&amp;amp;A, product launches), modeling the impact before decisions are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Partnership &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with RTM leaders and their GTM Ops partners across Direct, Expansion, and Benefits to ensure segmentation, book, quota, and capacity decisions reflect real operational context, while retaining ownership of the outcome and the execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with GTM Ops, Finance, and Sales Compensation to stay aligned with org-wide segmentation frameworks, revenue targets, and comp design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and proactively with sales leadership on plan status, tradeoffs, and risk: you&#39;re the trusted authority on &quot;how the books, quotas, and headcount are built and why.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document methodology and decisions so segmentation, quota, and capacity models are transparent, auditable, and repeatable across planning cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s what we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in Sales Ops, RevOps, or a similar analytical GTM role, with direct, hands-on experience owning segmentation, territory/book design, quota setting, or headcount/capacity planning; ideally in a fast-paced SaaS or fintech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to own outcomes and execution, not just analysis or recommendations: you&#39;re comfortable being the accountable owner when a quota, book, or headcount plan is challenged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sales process &amp;amp; tooling proficiency: you can build and audit account assignment/routing logic, manage territory and book structures, and build reporting that leaders trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical depth; comfortable building and defending quantitative models (quota, capacity, segmentation) under time pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running planning processes on a recurring cadence (annual/quarterly quota setting, ongoing book rebalancing, headcount reviews) across multiple stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication; you can defend a model&#39;s methodology to GTM leaders and senior sales leadership, and hold your ground when a decision is unpopular but correct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A first-principles problem solver who can build a defensible model from ambiguous inputs and translate org-level strategy into concrete, rules-based execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong cross-functional partner, able to work closely with GTM leaders and GTM Ops peers without ceding ownership of the outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning segmentation, book-of-business, or quota/capacity planning across multiple sales organizations or motions simultaneously (e.g., new business, expansion, and a distinct product line).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payroll, HR tech, benefits, or SMB SaaS go-to-market motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Sales Compensation and Finance on quota-to-comp alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or improving account assignment/routing automation (e.g., lead-routing tools, rules engines).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our cash compensation amount for this role is targeted at $100,000 - $120,000/yr in Scottsdale, $105,000 - $130,000/yr in Denver and Atlanta, $130,000 - $155,000/yr in San Francisco and New York, and $120,000 - $145,000 CAD/yr for Toronto. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate experience and expertise and may vary from the amounts listed above.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Gusto, we don&#39;t use titles the traditional way, as a signal of rank or hierarchy. Instead, our titles describe two things at once — your craft (what you do, e.g. Engineering, Design) and your scope of ownership (what you&#39;re accountable for) — which is why you&#39;ll see something like &quot;Head of X&quot; instead of a rank word like &quot;Director&quot; that tells you neither. Because of this, the title on this posting may look different from what you&#39;d expect based on the scope and seniority of the role, and from how similar roles are typically titled elsewhere. If you have questions about how this role compares to your current title or level, your recruiter can help translate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto has physical office spaces in Denver, San Francisco, and New York City. Employees who are based in those locations will be expected to work from the office on designated days approximately 2-3 days per week (or more depending on role). The same office expectations apply to all Symmetry roles, Gusto&#39;s subsidiary, whose physical office is in Scottsdale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: The San Francisco office expectations encompass both the San Francisco and San Jose metro areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When approved to work from a location other than a Gusto office, a secure, reliable, and consistent internet connection is required. This includes non-office days for hybrid employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliable, consistent presence: &lt;/strong&gt;We expect regular and predictable attendance, whether you&#39;re working in-office, hybrid, or fully remote, so that you stay closely connected to your team, customers, and stakeholders in real time and ensure colleagues and customers receive the timely support and responsiveness they deserve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our customers come from all walks of life and so do we. We hire great people from a wide variety of backgrounds, not just because it&#39;s the right thing to do, but because it makes our company stronger. If you share our values and our enthusiasm for small businesses, you will find a home at Gusto.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gusto is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Gusto considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Gusto is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. We want to see our candidates perform to the best of their ability. If you require a medical or religious accommodation at any time throughout your candidate journey, please fill out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdEfl7Bp-Twz7LLlhGlha46CrxZ9Kacgakmarf3K2TbnaEgKQ/viewform&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt; and a member of our team will get in touch with you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto takes security and protection of your personal information very seriously. Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/fraudulent-activity-disclaimer&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Disclaimer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personal information collected and processed as part of your Gusto application will be subject to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Gusto&#39;s Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Investment Designer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you dream about creating worlds imbued with real value and consequence? Can you imagine reward chases that excite and delight players without feeling like chores? Can you devise ways for players to meaningfully express themselves?&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt; If you answered yes to these questions, Bungie wants you on our team as our newest Senior Investment Designer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with an interdisciplinary team to create a wide variety of pursuit and reward-based systems &amp;amp; content that complement Marathon’s activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform advanced scripting and tool work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and create sustainable systems &amp;amp; content that excite and engage players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design creative additions and improvements for existing Rewards and Commerce systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tune gameplay values to create compelling moments and a satisfying progression curve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience as a designer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with game development software and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building rewards, player customization, and MTX systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning features or leading small teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to work as part of a large team and ability to take feedback and direction appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE-TO-HAVE SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience writing text-based scripts to manage game systems (scripting in a Lua, Python, or similar language)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple shipped game systems within the console or pc space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on games as a service/live content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$124,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$149,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord has a highly engaged community of millions of daily active users who use the platform for many different reasons, but there’s one thing that nearly everyone does: &lt;strong&gt;play video games.&lt;/strong&gt; Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming, and we are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to hang out before, during, and after playing games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord’s mission is to give people the power to create space to find belonging in their lives. Every day, millions of people trust Discord to be a place where they can talk, spend time together, and build community. Keeping that space safe starts with teams like ours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discord’s Violent Actors Team, part of the broader Threat Operations organization within Trust &amp;amp; Safety, identifies and disrupts violent and extremist actors and networks. As Threat Investigations Team Lead, you will manage and develop a team of investigators and analysts responsible for detecting, investigating, and disrupting ongoing and emerging threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a player-coach: setting a high bar for investigative quality while staying close enough to the work to guide complex cases and incident response. You will help early-career investigators build their tradecraft, turn investigative findings into actionable intelligence, and collaborate with internal and external partners during high-risk incidents. You will report to the team’s Senior Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is US-based and can be remote but if you live in the Bay Area, you&#39;re welcome to work from our beautiful SF office. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, coach, and develop a small team of investigators and analysts, setting clear expectations and providing timely, actionable feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team’s investigative quality, workload prioritization, queue health, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the first point of escalation for complex, ambiguous, or high-risk investigations, helping the team make sound and well-documented decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a player-coach: guide deep-dive network investigations, build the team’s tradecraft across case development, network analysis, proactive detection, and intelligence production, and help the team identify new detection and disruption opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate investigative signals and subject-matter expertise into recommendations about threat prioritization, policy gaps, and enforcement interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with law enforcement, government, industry, and other external partners when investigations or incidents require external engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hiring, onboarding, performance management, and career development while fostering an inclusive, resilient, and sustainable team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Should Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in threat intelligence, investigations, incident response, or a related field, with at least 2 years of prior people-management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in at least one extremist or violent-threat-actor ecosystem, with the analytical flexibility to develop proficiency across new harm areas as priorities evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to coach investigators, raise quality standards, deliver constructive feedback, and support the growth of people at different stages of their careers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in ambiguous, fast-changing situations — including defining scope, proposing solutions, and driving work to completion with limited oversight — while balancing immediate harm reduction against policy, legal, operational, and company-risk considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with investigative and case-management tooling, and the ability to use data and detection signals to guide team priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to translate complex and sensitive subjects for non-expert audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to cross-functional work, with the ability to build consensus and coordinate across teams, disciplines, and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting teams that regularly work with sensitive or potentially disturbing material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional language proficiency, particularly in languages relevant to high-harm threat-actor communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting complex threat findings to senior leaders or external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position is US-based and can be remote but if you live in the Bay Area, you’re welcome to work from our beautiful SF office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. This position will also be eligible for equity and benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role and level. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Please note that the compensation details listed in role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include equity, or benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$132,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$148,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Discord?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We&#39;re a multiplatform, multigenerational and multiplayer platform that helps people deepen their friendships around games and shared interests, and helps developers build and grow their businesses. We believe games give us a way to have fun with our favorite people, whether listening to music together or grinding in competitive matches for diamond rank. &lt;strong&gt;Join us in our mission! Your future is just a click away!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discord is committed to inclusion and providing reasonable accommodations during the interview process. &lt;/strong&gt;We want you to feel set up for success, so if you are in need of reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please see our Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy for details regarding Discord’s collection and usage of personal information relating to the application and recruitment process by clicking&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://discord.com/terms/applicant-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;HERE.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world&#39;s best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing at Brex&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marketing tells the story of Brex to the world. From acquisition to activation, we translate product value into business results. Our team spans Revenue, Product, and Brand Marketing, and works closely with nearly every function at Brex. We move fast, experiment often, and think deeply about customer behavior. If you want your creativity to drive growth and shape perception, this is the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brex is looking for a strategic, data-driven Senior Field Marketing Manager to build and lead the field marketing motion for our Commercial segment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial represents one of Brex&#39;s largest growth opportunities. This role will be responsible for developing the segment strategy, identifying the markets and audiences with the greatest potential, and creating integrated programs that generate new pipeline and accelerate existing opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate as the marketing lead for the Commercial business, partnering closely with Sales to understand their goals, test new approaches, and build repeatable programs that can scale. Your campaigns may include executive and customer events, industry programs, direct mail, digital experiences, partner activations, webinars, account-based plays, and other creative approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong commercial judgment with hands-on execution. You are comfortable analyzing pipeline and campaign performance, presenting to Sales leadership, and managing multiple campaigns and stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j03 paragraph&quot;&gt;This role will be fully remote and based in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the field marketing strategy, annual plan, budget, and pipeline goals for the Commercial segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial Sales leadership and set the planning rhythm across Marketing, Sales, and SDR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze account, pipeline, industry, geographic, and performance data to identify the highest-potential audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrated campaigns that combine in-person, digital, partner, content, direct mail, and account-based tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape event strategy, from regional programs to targeted dinners. For larger experiences, partner with the Events team while owning the audience, objective, Sales plan, and pipeline outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test new campaign ideas, define success upfront, and turn what works into repeatable plays and documented playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track results (pipeline, conversion, ROI) and present them to senior Marketing and Sales leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in B2B field marketing, demand gen, account-based marketing, or a related role, ideally in SaaS, fintech, or another high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning marketing strategy for a defined customer segment, region, industry, or sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of sourcing and accelerating pipeline through integrated programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of the B2B sales cycle and the ability to translate Sales priorities into focused marketing strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in marketing and pipeline metrics, including the ability to analyze campaign performance, diagnose gaps, and clearly explain results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and executive communication skills, with comfort juggling multiple programs in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 40% for events, Sales meetings, and customer programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a field marketing motion or entering an underdeveloped segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to companies in the Commercial or emerging mid-market segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with finance, fintech, spend, payments, ERP, or procurement audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Salesforce and marketing analytics platforms to assess funnel performance and campaign impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a business case for additional investment or team growth based on demonstrated results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is &lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;$116,000 - $165,000&lt;/span&gt;. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://brex.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://brex.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;brex.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Gusto&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Gusto, we&#39;re on a mission to grow the small business economy. We handle the hard stuff — payroll, health insurance, 401(k)s, and HR — so owners can focus on their craft and their customers. With teams in Denver, San Francisco, and New York, we support more than 500,000 small businesses nationwide and are building a workplace that reflects the people we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All full-time employees receive competitive base pay, benefits, and equity (RSUs) — because everyone who helps build Gusto should share in its success. Offer amounts are determined by role, level, and location. Learn more about our&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/total-rewards&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt; &lt;u&gt;Total Rewards philosophy&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is a fundamental part of how work gets done at Gusto. We expect all team members to actively engage with AI tools relevant to their role and grow their fluency as the technology evolves. AI experience requirements vary by role and will be assessed during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payments at Gusto aren&#39;t just infrastructure — they&#39;re the reason people get paid on time, every time. Payment Operations sits within Gusto&#39;s Money team, a cross-functional group spanning Engineering, Product, and Operations that powers money movement across Gusto&#39;s growing product surface: core payroll, contractor payments, international money movement, and new business offerings like PEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Payment Operations Analyst, you&#39;ll own specific end-to-end payment workflows, resolve exceptions that require real judgment, and help make our systems more reliable and efficient over time. Gusto&#39;s payment surface area is expanding — and this team is at the center of that growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who can shift from investigating a single misfired transaction to coordinating a response on a payment outage affecting thousands — and bring the same rigor to both. You think in systems. You hold partners accountable. You lead with curiosity and embrace AI as a core part of how you work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll collaborate closely with Engineering, Product, Accounting, Risk, and CX — and you&#39;ll develop strong day-to-day relationships with Gusto&#39;s bank and payment partners. When something breaks or slows down, you&#39;re the one who drives it to resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what you’ll do day-to-day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support the payment lifecycle end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational layer of specific payment workflows — ACH processing, exception handling, refunds, collection re-debits, reconciliation. When something is off, you investigate, escalate where needed, and see it through to resolution. And when you see a pattern, you push to fix the root cause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build alongside Product and Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment Operations doesn&#39;t just react — we shape how the systems work. You&#39;ll contribute to product specs, surface operational pain points, help define requirements, and participate in launches. You&#39;re a partner in building, not just a consumer of what gets shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the loop on customer pain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer and CX feedback is signal. You actively mine it to identify friction in payment flows, prioritize what matters, and bring those insights into the operational and product conversations where decisions get made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think in systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the dots across rails, partners, reconciliation, compliance, and customer experience. When an issue surfaces, you understand how it ripples — and you bring that perspective to cross-functional conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold partners to a high standard&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Gusto&#39;s bank and payment partners — domestic and international — to triage issues, resolve escalations, and maintain strong working relationships. You know how to be firm and collaborative at the same time, and you don&#39;t let things sit.&lt;br&gt;Lead with AI&lt;br&gt;You use AI as a genuine work partner — to move faster on analysis, draft communications, synthesize data, and automate the repetitive. You&#39;re always looking for the smarter way to get to the answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in payment operations, banking operations, treasury operations, or a related role at a fintech or financial institution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of domestic payment rails (ACH/Nacha, wires, RTP) and/or international money movement (cross-border transfers, FX, global disbursement networks); experience across both is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts — you look for the pattern behind the problem and can query or structure data to find it (SQL a plus but not required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with bank portals, payment processors, or reconciliation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate clearly with both operational and technical counterparts; you can write a crisp Slack to an engineer and a professional escalation to a bank partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in ambiguity and taking ownership without waiting for perfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eager to build AI into how you work — whether you&#39;re already using it daily or just getting started, you see it as a genuine productivity lever and are committed to developing that fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of relevant compliance frameworks (Nacha operating rules, unclaimed property, money transmission) is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our cash compensation amount for this role is targeted at $78,000-$97,000 /yr in Denver &amp;amp; most remote locations, and $97,000-$121,000 /yr for San Francisco, Seattle &amp;amp; New York. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors, including candidate experience and expertise, and may vary from the amounts listed above.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Gusto, we don&#39;t use titles the traditional way, as a signal of rank or hierarchy. Instead, our titles describe two things at once — your craft (what you do, e.g. Engineering, Design) and your scope of ownership (what you&#39;re accountable for) — which is why you&#39;ll see something like &quot;Head of X&quot; instead of a rank word like &quot;Director&quot; that tells you neither. Because of this, the title on this posting may look different from what you&#39;d expect based on the scope and seniority of the role, and from how similar roles are typically titled elsewhere. If you have questions about how this role compares to your current title or level, your recruiter can help translate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto has physical office spaces in Denver, San Francisco, and New York City. Employees who are based in those locations will be expected to work from the office on designated days approximately 2-3 days per week (or more depending on role). The same office expectations apply to all Symmetry roles, Gusto&#39;s subsidiary, whose physical office is in Scottsdale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: The San Francisco office expectations encompass both the San Francisco and San Jose metro areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When approved to work from a location other than a Gusto office, a secure, reliable, and consistent internet connection is required. This includes non-office days for hybrid employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliable, consistent presence: &lt;/strong&gt;We expect regular and predictable attendance, whether you&#39;re working in-office, hybrid, or fully remote, so that you stay closely connected to your team, customers, and stakeholders in real time and ensure colleagues and customers receive the timely support and responsiveness they deserve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our customers come from all walks of life and so do we. We hire great people from a wide variety of backgrounds, not just because it&#39;s the right thing to do, but because it makes our company stronger. If you share our values and our enthusiasm for small businesses, you will find a home at Gusto.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gusto is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Gusto considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Gusto is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. We want to see our candidates perform to the best of their ability. If you require a medical or religious accommodation at any time throughout your candidate journey, please fill out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdEfl7Bp-Twz7LLlhGlha46CrxZ9Kacgakmarf3K2TbnaEgKQ/viewform&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt; and a member of our team will get in touch with you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto takes security and protection of your personal information very seriously. Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/fraudulent-activity-disclaimer&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Disclaimer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personal information collected and processed as part of your Gusto application will be subject to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Gusto&#39;s Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the Director of MENA Public Policy you will develop and implement an engagement strategy with key policymakers, stakeholders, and opinion leaders across MENA. The successful candidate will oversee critical issues including, but not limited to, gaming, child safety, artificial intelligence, privacy, and consumer protection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a strategic thinker, driven to develop and execute creative strategies that advance Roblox’s business and priorities within the region. This position is based in Dubai and reports directly to the Head of Public Policy, Europe and MENA. The Director of MENA Public Policy will play a critical part in shaping Roblox&#39;s future in the country by establishing and executing effective public policy strategies. This role is instrumental in ensuring compliance, addressing policy issues, and fostering strong relationships with external partners, ultimately contributing to a safer and more engaging environment for Roblox&#39;s global community of developers and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and build relationships with regional policymakers and political figures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, monitor, and analyze policy issues affecting Roblox in MENA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute policy strategies around issues important to Roblox&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the wider public policy team on ongoing projects and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Roblox internal stakeholders on policy matters as inputs to the development of our products and business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate Roblox’s public policy positions and produce briefing papers and consultation responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empowered to fully pursue both your personal life and career goals, with support to take on increasing responsibilities and calculated risks for growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or higher in Political Science, Public Policy, Law, International Relations, Media, Technology, or related field of study or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience working with policymakers and stakeholders in MENA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the MENA policymaking and public opinion process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in intelligence collection and analysis, strategy development, project management, cross-functional partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, verbal and written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about public policy issues in MENA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solutions-driven and results-oriented strategic thinker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dynamic and engaging presenter with stellar oral delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, with strong communication, planning and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, with the ability to define your own work and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player, who values collaboration and partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a professional who approaches every individual as a client, regardless of their position, maintaining a calm and professional demeanor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with sales and pre-sales teams to drive pipeline and revenue targets, while also educating the product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influencing the product roadmap. You will develop deep relationships with senior customer business leaders and grow Stripe&#39;s solution offerings with new and existing customers. As a subject matter expert, you will scale the broader organization by creating reusable assets and coaching others on complex, high-value opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is looking for an online payments specialist with a proven track record of designing checkout experiences and payment flows for B2C and B2B enterprises. You will engage with Stripe&#39;s customers as a thought leader in the conversion optimization space, helping them understand how Stripe Link—Stripe&#39;s one-click checkout network—can reduce cart abandonment, improve returning customer conversion, and create a more seamless payments experience at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe Link to accelerate opportunities globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of checkout optimization, network-based authentication, and the business impact of saved payment methods on conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop expertise with Stripe&#39;s Link integration patterns—including embedded checkout, Stripe.js, and direct API flows—and guide customers through key implementation decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise customers on how Link interacts with the broader Stripe platform (Radar, Billing, Connect) to deliver compounding value across their payment stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, share, and learn best practices and reusable assets with the broader GTM organization to enhance the quality and efficiency of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reference architectures that help customers visualize end-to-end checkout and conversion improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Payments product sales team on Stripe&#39;s most strategic Link opportunities, leading solution strategy and owning key customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Link product team to get early exposure to new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; internally to drive product and feature request prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and summarize trends in checkout UX, wallets, passkeys, and network-based authentication, and provide actionable insights to product stakeholders and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point to drive complex technical issues to resolution with Stripe&#39;s engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on competitive analysis and market differentiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 25% travel is anticipated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a pre-sales, solutions architecture, or technical consulting role focused on online payments or e-commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of checkout optimization, including conversion metrics, cart abandonment, and the UX and technical levers that influence them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment authentication standards (3DS, passkeys, network tokenization) and their impact on authorization rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing payment flows and integrations for large enterprises, including multi-market and multi-currency scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering and API integration patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Stripe or other RESTful APIs into web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with A/B testing or analytics frameworks for checkout optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with wallet and one-click checkout ecosystems (Apple Pay, Google Pay, PayPal, Shop Pay)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a subject matter expert in a relevant industry, vertical, or product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world is having a monetization moment – every ambitious company is replatforming their billing solution in response to AI. Stripes Billing is a team of deep functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for one of the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Billing Sales is tasked with attacking a $100B market opportunity for automating the entire order to cash process and helping companies not get left behind in the AI era.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Head of Grower Sales (Billing),&amp;nbsp; you will use your leadership and management skills to manage and grow a team of Account Executives to drive expansion and retention of Stripe Billing across the AMER region. You will build and lead a team of sellers, while collaborating with the core sales leadership, marketing, product marketing, and product teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You will own the coaching, development, and performance of your team, driving the forecast of the business. You will be instrumental in leading in-depth product discussions with existing and prospective customers and building and executing against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of product sales executives focused on expansion and retention of our largest Billing Users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create go-to-market plans and solutions to meet our customer needs, in collaboration with Product, Sales, Finance and Marketing stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day operations, with a focus on performance against key sales metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for driving revenue, increasing attach rates, and new client acquisition at high rates of growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills through all facets of the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get hands on engaged in the largest, most strategic opportunities, leading executive relationships and helping the team win new customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and enable individual development to promote career growth of direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with clarity and context with a compelling plan in line with Stripe’s direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and focus for GTM ideas and product sales campaigns that the product team is exploring. Drive execution and measurement. Analyse results and make recommendations for action in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constantly innovate and improve programs and program management mechanisms, suggesting new ideas, sharing best practices, and improving the business and customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept sales leader, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization. You have a reputation and drive for building strategic relationships with executives (CEO, CFO, and CTO) across the AMER region, including core markets like NA, CA, and LATAM. You excel in building clear plans to grow a region through a high-functioning sales team, with strategic thought leadership and strong management. You see value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require both deep product understanding and technical knowledge, especially for AI industry users. You’re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives) and are excited to become an expert and share your knowledge. You possess an organized, self-starter mindset and excellent communication skills, with a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of sales leadership experience, launching and growing high-functioning sales teams/products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20+ years of experience in hyper-growth SaaS environments across the AMER region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in finance, revenue management, financial services, or similar software services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be a self-starter, capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves” mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke agreements with startup, SMB, and Commercial businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: Interaction Designer (Contract)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bungie is seeking an Interaction Designer to delight millions by designing amazing player interactions within Marathon. You’ll be responsible for producing UX design work on a cross functional team, evolving problems that are complex and ambiguous into clear actionable design solutions. You&#39;ll work from concept to completion by collaborating closely with other designers to achieve your goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert goals and requirements into viable solutions that follow and complement our UX strategy and design principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize appropriate UX design methodologies to communicate and validate the player experience: player interviews, flow diagrams, playtesting, high-fidelity mockups, and prototypes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and document strategies, guidelines, and patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Effective collaborator&lt;/em&gt;: You know how to move a design forward with your team and in discussions with stakeholders using proven collaboration methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;User-centered designer&lt;/em&gt;: You are a committed believer in putting player needs at the center of the development process. You know how to incorporate both qualitative and quantitative insights into your design process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Visual communicator&lt;/em&gt;: You have comprehensive knowledge of graphic design fundamentals like layout, color theory and typography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Process and team driven&lt;/em&gt;: You can break experiences down with a team to ship value to our players. You embrace that an effective user experience needs feedback and iteration to achieve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Systematic thinker&lt;/em&gt;: Your design process considers moderate-to-large scale solutions that are sustainable over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a cross-functional product team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio with UX projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Have Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Human-Computer Interaction, User Experience, Cognitive Science or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in games across multiple platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use design software (Figma, Adobe Suite, etc.) to convey designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with player onboarding systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At SIE, working with our partners, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the individual base pay range may vary based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role is eligible for benefit offerings that include medical, dental, and vision. Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dzconnex.com/summary-of-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below, this is an hourly rate.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$67.69&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$81.44 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Bungie Publishing team is seeking a Principal Marketing Manager (Contract) to lead integrated global go-to-market strategy and planning for Marathon. Reporting to the Director, Marathon Franchise Marketing, this role will translate franchise strategy, product roadmaps, audience insights, and business objectives into cohesive marketing plans that acquire new players, reengage existing owners, and deepen the commitment of Marathon’s active community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as a senior cross-functional leader across Brand, Product Marketing, Growth, Community, Communications, Creative, Analytics, Finance, regional teams, and Development. The ideal candidate combines strategic judgment with operational leadership: someone who can create clarity from complexity, align senior stakeholders around difficult decisions, and continually improve our plans through player insight and performance data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Own the development of integrated global GTM strategies for major Marathon releases, seasons, and franchise moments, ensuring plans support franchise priorities, player needs, and business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Translate franchise strategy, product roadmaps, audience priorities, and business objectives into clear marketing strategies, launch architectures, milestones, and investment recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Develop audience-led plans spanning acquisition, reactivation, retention, engagement, and long-term player value across paid, owned, earned, community, platform, and regional channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Establish and lead the cross-functional GTM operating rhythm, including planning milestones, readiness reviews, decision points, dependency management, risk tracking, and post-launch learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Align senior stakeholders and executional partners around priorities, roles, tradeoffs, and success measures, ensuring critical information and decisions are communicated clearly and consistently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Identify GTM risks and opportunities early, develop actionable recommendations, and drive timely resolution across Publishing, Development, and regional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Partner with Brand and Creative teams to translate Marathon’s positioning and creative strategy into consistent, audience-relevant campaigns and player experiences across channels and markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Partner with regional marketing teams to adapt global strategies for North America, EMEA, APAC, and LATAM while maintaining a cohesive franchise approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Partner with Analytics, Insights, Product Management, and Finance to establish audience targets, performance benchmarks, measurement plans, and budget-efficiency goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Define, monitor, and report against franchise and campaign KPIs, including awareness, consideration, acquisition, conversion, reactivation, retention, engagement, revenue, and ROI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Lead marketing performance reviews and translate player, market, and campaign insights into optimization plans that inform future campaigns, product beats, and investment decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Guide global paid media strategy, budget allocation, and agency partnerships as part of the broader integrated GTM plan, optimizing investment across channels, audiences, and regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Partner with Product Management and Development to unlock value from first-party platform relationships and identify opportunities that strengthen reach, engagement, and commercial performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Provide clear direction to agencies, vendors, and executional partners through strong briefs, aligned scopes, disciplined budget management, and timely feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 7+ Years experience leading integrated marketing, product marketing, or GTM strategy within gaming, technology, entertainment, or another complex consumer business; experience operating at a global scale is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Demonstrated success leading complex, cross-functional launches or live-service marketing programs with meaningful audience and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Deep familiarity with game franchises and online player communities, ideally within first-person shooters, extraction shooters, or live-service games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Strong understanding of the full marketing mix, including brand, product marketing, community, communications, creative, partnerships, lifecycle marketing, organic channels, paid media, and player acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Ability to translate product strategy, audience insight, and business goals into clear GTM choices, integrated plans, and investment recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Proven ability to influence senior leaders, align teams without direct authority, and resolve competing priorities across complex organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Strong analytical and commercial judgment, with experience defining success measures and using performance data, research, and player insight to improve strategy and execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Exceptional written, verbal, and presentation communication skills, with the ability to make complex topics clear, compelling, and actionable for executive and cross-functional audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Demonstrated ability to create clarity across multiple complex workstreams, establish priorities and decision points, and drive stakeholders toward timely resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Sound judgment and adaptability when navigating changing product plans, emerging player sentiment, competitive disruption, or other high-pressure business challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice-to-Have Skills&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Deep familiarity with Marathon, its evolving player community, and the broader competitive landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Expertise marketing live-service games across launch, seasonal, reactivation, and long-term lifecycle moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Experience developing global strategies that can be effectively adapted for regional markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Experience managing major media investments, external agencies, and first-party platform partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At SIE, working with our partners, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the individual base pay range may vary based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role is eligible for benefit offerings that include medical, dental, and vision. Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dzconnex.com/summary-of-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below, this is an hourly rate.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$79&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$89 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Operations team is responsible for the systems, processes, and data infrastructure that power Stripe&#39;s global marketing engine. We partner closely with Growth, Demand Generation, Regional Marketing, Lifecycle, Sales Development, and Marketing Technology teams to ensure campaigns are executed with precision, prospect data is accurate and actionable, and our marketing technology stack operates at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are systems thinkers and operational leaders focused on improving the workflows, tooling, data quality, and processes that enable marketing and sales teams to move faster and more effectively. Our work spans campaign operations, marketing automation, prospect data management, and cross-functional program delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Program Manager to lead cross-functional programs that grow Stripe&#39;s reach to new businesses in direct support of Stripe’s mission. This role sits at the intersection of technology, data, and program management, and it requires someone who can move fluidly between strategic planning and hands-on execution via deep partnerships with engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as a process owner for key marketing and sales development operations work streams, partnering with stakeholders in marketing, sales development, product, and engineering to deliver scalable solutions that improve efficiency, data quality, and pipeline impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsibilities can include the following and will vary by area of coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and lead programs to build an agentic acquisition program for how Stripe engages with prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end program delivery for initiatives; maintain program communications, track milestones, lead cross-functional workstreams, and provide regular updates on roadmap progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programs to address recurring sales development and/or marketing operational challenges; define objectives, success metrics, and build repeatable processes that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketing, product and engineering teams to scope business requirements, coordinate discovery, and translate operational needs into product requirements for internal tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate review cycles, pilots, and feedback collection during program execution; summarize required changes, identify launch-blocking issues, and escalate risks as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive ongoing operations improvements through process innovation, automation, and the adoption of AI-powered tools to increase productivity and transform workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain scalable documentation and support coordination with offshore production teams and cross-functional partners across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in B2B marketing/sales/revenue operations or a related program management role in a high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience working day-to-day with marketing automation platforms, CRM platforms, prospect data, and lead management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in end-to-end program management of cross-functional marketing, sales, and engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI agents, including examples of agents you have deployed and examples of ways you are using AI on a daily basis beyond chat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience doing your own analysis using queries, dashboards, and AI and partnering with analysts and data scientists for more complex analytics needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience defining your own scope and goals and collaborating with a distributed, global team to deliver on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to convey complex operational concepts to diverse stakeholders across marketing, sales, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with Salesforce or Marketo, including lead and contact management, campaign attribution, and marketing-to-sales data flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing AI tools to improve marketing operations workflows and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global teams on a day-to-day basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the financial services, payments, or B2B software industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Ecosystem Partnerships team builds the partner ecosystem that helps users discover, adopt, and get more value from Stripe. We work with a broad range of technology, platform, and ecosystem partners, and collaborate closely with Partner Engineering, Product Marketing, Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams to bring Stripe’s products to market through partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Development Manager (PDM), you will help manage and grow a long tail of partners that make up the Stripe ecosystem. You will create and manage the programs, partner tiers, operating rhythms, and enablement needed to support partners at scale - not simply one relationship at a time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help partners understand and adopt new Stripe primitives, product capabilities, and integration opportunities. You will turn partner feedback and market context into clear priorities, coordinate cross-functional work, and ensure that partner programs are effective, measurable, and easy to engage with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys building scalable programs, bringing structure to ambiguous work, and enabling many partners to succeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a broad portfolio of ecosystem partners through scalable programs, tiers, communications, and operating mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design, launch, and operate partner programs that provide clear value to partners and advance Stripe’s ecosystem and product priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain partner tiering, engagement models, program criteria, and lifecycle motions that make it easier to prioritize support and scale partner impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of new Stripe primitives, product capabilities, and partner-facing initiatives across the ecosystem. Develop partner enablement plans and track adoption, engagement, and delivery against defined KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Partner Engineering to surface partner integration needs, identify recurring technical or product friction, coordinate enablement, and improve the partner integration experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product Marketing to develop partner messaging, launches, education, and campaigns that help partners understand Stripe’s value proposition and take action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, Operations, PE&amp;amp;O, RPS, and other stakeholders to translate partner insights into clear workstreams, resolve blockers, and execute effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track partner health, program performance, commitments, and delivery milestones. Use data and qualitative feedback to identify opportunities to improve program design, partner experience, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support templated deals, renewals, and other well-defined commercial workstreams using established strategies and processes; escalate material changes, risks, and blockers through the appropriate operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong understanding of the ecosystem, partner objectives and constraints, Stripe’s product capabilities, and relevant market developments. Share material insights and recommendations with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive relationships across Stripe and with partners, communicate clearly, and help align stakeholders with competing priorities around shared outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to an inclusive, high-performing team culture and apply Stripe’s operating principles in day-to-day work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a thoughtful, execution-oriented partnerships professional who is energized by operating at scale. You enjoy building programs, defining tiers and operating models, and improving the systems that enable many partners to succeed. You can build context quickly, turn it into clear plans, and collaborate well across functions with different goals and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are equally comfortable engaging partners directly and identifying patterns across a portfolio. You exercise sound judgment within established frameworks, communicate proactively, and know when to seek input or escalate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, account management, strategic programs, go-to-market, or a comparable cross-functional role involving external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, operating, or improving scalable programs, partner tiers, lifecycle motions, or other systems that serve a broad portfolio of customers or partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple workstreams, establish clear plans and milestones, and reliably deliver on commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills and a demonstrated ability to build alignment with stakeholders across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Operations, Go-to-Market, and/or comparable functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain product value, synthesize feedback, and keep internal and external stakeholders informed of material developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and operational rigor: comfort defining and tracking KPIs, assessing program and partner health, identifying risks or blockers, and using data and structured judgment to improve outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop productive relationships with external partners and to balance partner needs with Stripe’s priorities and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in Stripe’s products, our users, and the ecosystem in which we operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ecosystem, platform, technology, payments, financial-services, or SaaS partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving adoption of new product capabilities, integrations, or platform primitives through partner enablement, education, or go-to-market programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with partner-facing engineering, product, or product-marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with partner integrations, commercial agreements, partner operations, or risk and compliance considerations in a regulated or complex environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is a team of performance-driven marketers and channel specialists. We partner closely with growth, creative, analytics, and regional marketing to drive revenue through self-serve and sales motions. We work globally, across all Stripe offerings and with all company segments - from startups to the largest enterprises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In this role, you’d be joining a global, cross-functional team dedicated to testing and scaling cutting-edge acquisition channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our team helps Stripe increase the GDP of the internet by ensuring our web presence is perfectly optimized for the next generation of artificial intelligence and search technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an AEO and GEO Marketing Manager to lead the channel. This individual will play a critical role in growing new user acquisition from platforms including ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews. The scope of the role includes Generative Engine Optimization (GEO), also known as Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) or Large Language Model (LLM) Search Optimization, improving AI agent experience, and integrating AI capabilities to improve the performance and efficiency of search and answer engine channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will spearhead efforts by developing and executing a roadmap of activities and experiments to improve answer engine performance. They will have the opportunity to work closely with cross-functional partners including Growth Marketing, Content Marketing, Engineering, and Analytics at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the growth and user acquisition strategy for the Answer Engine Optimization channel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Stripe.com so artificial intelligence agents can efficiently access and take action on behalf of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead the development and integration of artificial intelligence capabilities to improve the efficiency of search and answer engine channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular reports and updates on channel performance to track progress and identify new opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with content, engineering, and data analytics teams to build a comprehensive testing roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience creating and executing search engine optimization strategies, with direct experience with answer engine optimization and generative engine optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven technical experience making websites SEO and AEO-friendly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing data and in dashboards and reporting software such as Tableau, Looker, Adobe Analytics, or Google Analytics to drive growth decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying user intent analysis to prioritize actions that deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to take initiative, independently problem-solve, and drive tasks to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading project roadmaps across cross-functional stakeholders, including engineering and content teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or familiarity with Natural Language Processing (NLP), vector search, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing search optimization in-house for business-to-business (B2B) software-as-a-service (SaaS) companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within the fintech, payments, billing, accounting, or startup industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing SQL queries to extract and gather data independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or 4 years of additional relevant professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is responsible for driving organizational effectiveness and leading transformational programs across Marketing, Self-serve, Startup and Sales Development. We create the processes and conditions that enable high performance across teams and help Stripe scale with focus and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We partner closely with the CMO, Marketing and Sales Development leadership team to define strategy, lead operational planning, and steward execution across global programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work spans cross-functional efforts that are critical to Stripe’s growth. From delivering strategic insights and frameworks to leading complex initiatives, we focus on what moves the needle most for the business. We care about results, not activity, and we have fun doing it. If you like hard problems, are analytical, and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Campaign Strategy &amp;amp; Operations Manager, you&#39;ll own the operational foundation that powers Stripe&#39;s global demand engine — building the systems, processes, and workflows that enable our marketing teams to move faster and perform better at scale. You&#39;ll partner with the Global Campaigns, Demand, and Field Marketing teams to drive strategic planning, design operational processes such as budget management and resource planning, and collaborate across global, regional, and channel teams to execute the end-to-end campaign lifecycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility, high-impact role at the intersection of marketing strategy and operational execution — one where the work you build today shapes how the entire demand function operates for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Campaigns, Demand and Field Marketing leadership team on operating cadences and processes, including monthly and quarterly business reviews, annual planning, budget and resource allocation, org-wide goal setting, and communications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global, regional, and channel teams to architect and implement scalable operating models to support the end-to-end campaign &amp;amp; event lifecycle, from initial strategy and planning through execution, measurement, and optimization, ensuring seamless integration across various functions and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently monitor and analyze the campaign production &amp;amp; activation &quot;supply chain&quot; including tracking all key stages, handoffs, and friction points to drive meaningful efficiency gains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently scope and lead strategic programs to solve high-impact problems. This includes developing frameworks, aligning stakeholders, and ensuring execution drives measurable outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and report out on key operational metrics and team performance, clearly communicating the health of the campaign &amp;amp; event supply chain, the impact of operational improvements, and the overall effectiveness of campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage campaign and event analytics to do ad-hoc, deep-dives on user engagement patterns, conversion trends, and growth opportunities across the demand funnel. Use these insights to shape hypotheses, drive prioritization conversations, and identify areas to probe more deeply in partnership with Marketing, Finance and GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clarity to ambiguity. You’ll navigate complexity, distill insight from noise, resolve issues quickly, and empower teams to make smart, confident decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of demand generation, campaign &amp;amp; marketing operations, strategy and operations, business operations, or similar roles with exposure to both business and technical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in partnering with regional teams and channel partners to build scalable, end-to-end demand generation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deploy AI-powered solutions within campaigns or demand generation with specific, measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross-functional settings, and in a role that spans strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation, writing, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appetite and ability to work through ambiguity with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change management background and ability to influence diverse stakeholder groups across global, regional, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of marketing and how its varied disciplines work together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management tools such as Asana, Monday.com, or Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Marketing automation systems and tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, finance, fintech, or high-growth technology companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in management consulting or program management roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk team helps maintain a healthy financial ecosystem for businesses around the world. Credit Operations conducts credit risk assessments, underwrites small and mid-sized users, and develops mitigation strategies that enable Stripe to take smart risks while supporting growth. The globally distributed team partners with stakeholders across regions to support new and existing users and products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Credit Operations Manager, you will lead and develop a team of credit operations analysts while setting a strategic vision for scalable, high-quality operations. You will help enable new and existing Stripe products by translating product strategies into operational capabilities and appropriate credit controls. In partnership with Credit Strategy, Product, Engineering, and Data Science, you will launch new programs and advance AI-enabled automation across Credit Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, motivate, and develop a high-performing Credit Operations team by setting clear goals, providing regular coaching and feedback, and supporting professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the team’s current and future capability needs and partner on hiring, workforce planning, and development strategies to close material gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities for the team in alignment with Credit’s broader strategy and translate them into clear goals, work plans, and operating mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve Credit Operations’ systems, processes, and operating model to improve decision quality, mitigate emerging risks, and scale efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new and existing Stripe products by assessing credit and operational impacts, defining requirements and controls, and preparing Credit Operations for launch and ongoing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Risk leadership and cross-functional stakeholders to prioritize investments in risk mitigation, operational efficiency, and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools and partner with technical and operational stakeholders to test and implement automation, with appropriate quality controls and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage operating metrics and service-level agreements, using performance insights and root-cause analysis to drive improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee credit-related vendor performance and ensure work meets applicable quality and compliance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10-15 years of work experience in commercial credit underwriting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience leading credit risk or underwriting teams in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial risk modeling or cash-flow forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams, including setting goals, managing performance, and coaching team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate complex challenges into actionable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to influence across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, launching, and scaling programs, products, or operational capabilities from planning through implementation and measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-enabled tools and partnering with technical and operational stakeholders to implement automation, including quality controls, change management, and team adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to delivering a user-centered experience while effectively managing risk&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting credit-related product launches or translating product capabilities into operational requirements, workflows, controls, and launch-readiness plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of accounting principles and experience evaluating financial statements and business models across industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience analyzing data and creating dashboards using SQL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering teams to develop or improve investigative and decisioning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field; advanced degree or certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a versatile marketing leader to manage our marketing engagement across the Middle East, North Africa and Türkiye (MENAT). As our first local marketing person in the region, you will design and execute a comprehensive GTM strategy that accounts for the diverse cultural, economic, and linguistic landscape of MENAT.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for identifying high-growth clusters, navigating complex regulatory environments, and building a unified brand voice that resonates across multiple borders. Your work will span social, influencers, partner, and event marketing. You will be at the center of all the region&#39;s outbound activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; United Arab Emirates (plus a few weeks at HQ for an extended orientation)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Regional Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Design a scalable marketing framework that can be adapted for Tier 1 MENAT markets (high volume/established) and Tier 2/3 markets (high growth).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localized Content Ecosystem:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the &quot;transcreation&quot; and localization of all marketing assets. While English is our core working language, you will ensure our brand voice translates with native-level nuance across key MENAT regions, leveraging your fluent Arabic skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile GTM Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead product launches across MENAT, prioritizing markets based on data, barriers to entry, and localized product-market fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Border Community &amp;amp; Influencer Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage regional social media and platform trends to build a loyal community through targeted influencer partnerships and localized channels (Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policy &amp;amp; Comms Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with legal and policy teams to navigate the varied regulatory landscapes of MENAT, ensuring absolute compliance with local data privacy standards relevant to the MENAT region and local data privacy standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event &amp;amp; Ecosystem Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop locally relevant events and community initiatives across key priority MENAT markets, while also participating in existing industry events that support relationship building, market understanding and ecosystem growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Market Partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and develop trusted partnerships with brands, NGOs, across key MENAT markets to strengthen local credibility, relevance and long-term growth, while deepening engagement with creators, industry stakeholders and broader market ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of marketing experience&lt;/strong&gt; with a deep, pan-regional focus across MENAT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent Drive:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to operate autonomously within a strategic framework, driving clear outcomes with minimal day-to-day oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Proficiency: Fluent Arabic speaker is required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Broad Market Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing marketing efforts in highly fragmented environments—from varying audience demographics and cultural perceptions to distinct MENAT economic climates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years in Consumer Tech:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of the consumer journey, specifically privacy-first user behaviors, mobile trends, and local trust barriers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to advocate effectively for regional MENAT needs (budget, product localized features, compliance requirements) to a global/US-based HQ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven test and learn mentality:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to drive growth and iterate quickly by being resourceful, analytical, and hands-on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Law Enforcement Liaison (Kansas), you’ll develop and advance strategic law enforcement and safety relationships with special focus on law enforcement, while also supporting internal platform safety efforts that elevate the Roblox safety ecosystem. The ideal candidate will be a versatile, self-driven, team-player who enjoys context-switching across high-profile initiatives, and is uniquely motivated by Roblox’s mission of connecting a billion people with optimism and civility. From serving as an external representative of Roblox with state and local law enforcement agencies, to collaborating cross-functionally with our Legal &amp;amp; Advocacy, Civility, Safety, Product, and Communications teams (among others), you will have a diverse set of responsibilities in furtherance of assisting law enforcement, educating external stakeholders such as parents and educators on digital safety, and ultimately helping keep users safe on Roblox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is remotely based in Kansas and will report to the Senior Manager of US Public Policy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: This role requires On-Call support during weekends and holidays, and is expected to include frequent travel. The scope may also require reviewing graphic, controversial, and offensive content in accordance with Roblox’s handling policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and advance strategic law enforcement relationships with special focus on law enforcement in the State of Kansas, and Midwestern region, while assisting with global outreach as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with federal, state, and local law enforcement, including with the Kansas Attorney General’s Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute educational programs for law enforcement agencies and other key external stakeholders (i.e. parent groups and educators) regarding Roblox’s platform safety efforts, including our law enforcement response policies and NCMEC CyberTip initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify, monitor, analyze, and internally advise on law enforcement developments affecting Roblox in the State of Kansas and Midwestern region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek to understand and empathetically respond to regional law enforcement concerns, while helping internally codify and scale resultant learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listen to and understand the concerns of Kansas parents, caregivers, and educators regarding the safety of Roblox. You will provide guidance and education that empower these audiences and build confidence in Roblox’s emphasis on product and policy safety, which keeps users safe and healthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forge a deep subject-matter expertise of Roblox’s internal and external safety practices, so as to identify, advocate for, and help implement strategic safety enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft professional work product – for both internal and external audiences – supported by clear, concise, and multi-sourced platform safety investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and build strong internal relationships across our Legal &amp;amp; Advocacy, Safety, Product, and Communications teams (among others) to help address law enforcement emergencies, platform safety escalations, and comprehensive Roblox undertakings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of work experience in law enforcement, intelligence, government, trust and safety, or an adjacent field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed knowledge of the law enforcement community and related policymakers in the State of Kansas, and Midwestern region, along with current trends and challenges in online safety and policy (particularly child safety and regional-specific considerations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for and a demonstrated track record of stellar public speaking, short-notice travel, building and maintaining constructive relationships, defining your own work processes, and adding organizational value no matter how small or large the task.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication, leadership, and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agility to navigate ambiguity, resilience to overcome obstacles, and the internal drive to concurrently manage multiple high-profile, time-sensitive initiatives in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unwavering integrity, collegiality, and grit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel&#39;s sales team is built on people who are technically fluent, commercially sharp, and deeply curious about the companies they sell into.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll run full-cycle deals in close partnership with Solutions Architects, Marketing, and Customer Success, and you’ll help shape how Vercel goes to market as we continue to expand our Commercial segment. We’re building a team with a strong preference to grow talent internally. If you want a path to larger scopes and leadership over time, this is a great place to do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, net-new logo role on a fast-growing, technical sales team. You’ll sell to developers and engineering leaders at modern, digital-native companies, connecting Vercel’s front-end cloud and developer experience to measurable business outcomes (speed, conversion, productivity, reliability).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be at the leading edge of modern web and AI, working with customers who build and ship fast. You’ll collaborate closely with Solutions Architects, Marketing, Product, and Customer Success to help teams adopt Vercel and expand their impact as they scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a net-new revenue number by building and progressing pipeline from first meeting through close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline in partnership with your BDR and generate your own outbound pipeline through prospecting, multi-threading, and thoughtful account research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute territory and account plans to drive consistent new logo acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run end-to-end sales cycles: discovery, qualification, deal strategy, technical evaluation, stakeholder alignment, negotiation, and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a weekly forecast and maintain high pipeline hygiene (stages, next steps, close plans, CRM accuracy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of leading indicator metrics (e.g., activity, meetings, pipeline creation/conversion) and adjust your operating rhythm to consistently hit targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Solutions Architects and Customer Success to drive successful evaluations, strong handoffs, and the best outcomes for your customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on Vercel’s product and competitive landscape; translate technical value into clear business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use tools like Sales Navigator, ZoomInfo, Outreach, SFDC, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top performer with history of success in pipeline generation, opportunity management, and closing customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coachable and collaborative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team first attitude and no ego&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about your customers and how Vercel solves their problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated, curious, hungry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience helping companies in hyper-growth stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience in Product Led Growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience in Front End Software Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
