&lt;p&gt;Riot’s Anti-Cheat team is versatile and passionate about our craft. We understand the player impact of cheating in games and are focused on setting the highest bar for the integrity of multiplayer games. We relish the opportunity to work with new tech stacks and bring security to all of Riot&#39;s games; each with its own security risk profile and complex challenges. At the most fundamental level, our goal is to promote the best player experience by protecting the legitimacy of their favorite games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Anti-Cheat Engineering Manager &lt;/strong&gt;for Mobile Vanguard,&amp;nbsp; you will lead the team responsible for the ongoing development and evolution of Vanguard Anti-Cheat’s services on mobile. You’ll help set direction, shape priorities, and ensure the team delivers secure, reliable capabilities across Vanguard’s mobile suite in a timely manner. While your primary focus will be enabling the team and driving outcomes, your strong fluency in mobile security and cheat techniques will allow you to guide architecture, challenge technical decisions, and step directly into complex debugging or investigations when needed. You’ll help the team anticipate and analyze emerging cheat techniques, then translate those findings into effective detections, mitigations, and preventative controls. You will report to the Senior Engineering Manager of the Anti-Cheat&amp;nbsp; team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, identify, recruit, interview, and hire engineers to help the team scale effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set direction and drive high-impact anti-cheat capabilities from ambiguity through production to prevent cheating in mobile and console environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team in rapidly translating emerging threats into resilient detections and preventative countermeasures that can be safely deployed at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance immediate threat response with proactive technical investments that anticipate adversaries’ next moves or eliminate common abuse vectors entirely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with game teams across genres to understand their specific security needs and help shape the security landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote secure coding standards and design that reduce vectors for cheating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep up-to-date with the state of cheats and cheating techniques across mobile titles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support game teams directly in understanding cheating ecosystems and integrating Anti-Cheat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 4+ years of industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity or experience with Android and/or iOS platform security models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical understanding of mobile platforms (Android/iOS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying mobile native (C/C++) SDKs and/or frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Android and/or iOS build tools (Android SDK/NDK, Xcode, LLVM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Android &amp;amp; iOS executable formats, reverse engineering, or binary exploitation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile reverse engineering tools (Frida, IDA Pro, Radare2, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Gen9 Console (Xbox Series XS and/or PS5) development a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with macOS platform and security features a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise, a collaborative spirit, and choices that focus on your fellow Rioters, who are the customers of your work. Being a dedicated fan of games is not necessary for this position!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Riot focuses on work/life balance, shown by our open paid time off policy and other perks such as flexible work schedules. We offer medical, dental, and life insurance, parental leave for you, your spouse/domestic partner, and children, and a 401k with company match. Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/work-with-us/overview&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;benefits pages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Riot Games, we&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;put players first&lt;/a&gt;. That mission drives every decision in our quest to create games and experiences that make it better to be a player. Whether you’re working directly on a new player-facing experience or you’re supporting the company as a whole, everyone at Riot is part of our mission. And just like in our games, we’re better when we work together. Our goal is to create collaborative teams where you are empowered to bring your unique perspective everyday. If that sounds like the kind of place you want to work, we’re looking forward to your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;It’s our policy to provide equal employment opportunity for all applicants and members of Riot Games, Inc. Riot Games makes reasonable accommodations for handicapped and disabled Rioters and does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, handicap, veteran status, marital status, criminal history, or any other category protected by applicable federal and state law. We consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with criminal histories, in a manner consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including the California Fair Chance Act, the City of Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, the San&amp;nbsp;Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, and the Washington Fair Chance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Per the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance, the following core duties may create a basis for disqualifying candidates with relevant criminal histories:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Safeguarding confidential and sensitive Company data &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Communication with others, including Rioters and third parties such as vendors, and/or players, including minors&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accessing Company assets, secure digital systems, and networks&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensuring a safe interactive environment for players and other Rioters&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;These duties are directly related to essential operations, safety, trust, and compliance obligations within our organization. Please note that job duties may evolve based on business needs and additional responsibilities may be assigned as necessary to maintain operational efficiency and security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(Redwood City Only)&lt;/strong&gt; Base salary range between $246,300.00 - $343,400.00 USD + incentive compensation + equity + 401K with company match + medical, dental, vision, and life insurance + short and long-term disability + open PTO.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Content Strategy Lead for Executive Programs, you will own what Anthropic brings to the table when we sit down with senior leaders from our most strategic customers. That covers Executive Briefings, Customer Advisory Boards, Executive Councils, and the other small-room gatherings where a C-level audience meets with our leaders, product teams, and researchers. You will set the content strategy across these programs, build the library of modules and the bench of speakers, and lead the team that keeps our content fresh as our models and products evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role works cross-functionally with Product &amp;amp; Solutions Marketing, who owns positioning and messaging across industries and products, and customer programs which owns each program&#39;s operations, intake, and customer experience. You own the layer in between: turning Anthropic&#39;s product, research, and policy story into sessions built for an executive audience, deciding who is best placed to deliver them, and designing interactive formats and demos that work for customers building on the frontier.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right candidate has a product marketing or narrative background, has built content for C-level customer audiences at an enterprise technology company, and has managed a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Set and execute the content strategy across Executive Briefings, Customer Advisory Boards, Executive Councils, and other gatherings of strategic customers: the themes for the year, the narrative that connects them, and how content differs by program, audience, and purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain an evergreen library of content modules that program leads and account teams can assemble into an agenda without starting from scratch. Modules span product and roadmap, research, safety and policy, industry and use-case sessions, demos, and discussion guides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Keep the library current. Set a refresh cadence tied to model and product launches, retire what is stale, maintain a pipeline of net-new content modules, and make sure nothing in front of a customer executive is out of date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Identify, recruit, develop and certify speakers from Anthropic&#39;s executive, product, research, and go-to-market teams. Maintain the cross-program roster, shape each speaker&#39;s session, and prepare them for the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Design the experience, not only the presentation. Choose the format that fits the audience and the goal, whether that is a working session, a live demo, a conversation with a researcher, or a peer discussion among customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Partner with program leads on agendas for the highest-priority engagements, tailoring modules to the customer&#39;s objectives. Set the standards and templates that let every other engagement meet the same bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Work with Product &amp;amp; Solutions Marketing, Product, and Research so that executive-level content is ready when a launch happens, not weeks after.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Capture what customers say in these rooms, including themes, objections, and requests. Route it to Product, Research, Marketing, and go-to-market leadership, and use it to improve the content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Measure what works, including session feedback, module usage, and speaker performance, and work with program leads to connect content to program outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Hire, manage, and develop the team responsible for executive program content, and set its quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Use Claude to scale the work: build workflows that tailor modules to a customer&#39;s industry and priorities so a customized session does not require a rebuild.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Built content for C-level customer audiences in executive briefings, advisory boards, executive councils, or similar programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Built a content system that other people rely on, such as a module library, a session catalog, or a speaker program, and kept it current through frequent product change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;The technical fluency to work directly with researchers and engineers, understand what they have built, and explain it accurately to a business executive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience coaching senior executives and technical experts as speakers, including giving direct feedback on their material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Judgment about format: you know when a room needs a presentation, a demo, or a facilitated discussion, and you can design each one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience managing people, including hiring and developing a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;A high bar for writing. You can draft an executive session narrative yourself and improve one written by someone else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Genuine interest in AI and in helping the world&#39;s largest enterprises adopt it responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;12+ years in product marketing, executive content, or executive customer programs at a B2B technology company. You have owned positioning and messaging for a technical product and know how to adapt it for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience at a company where the product changes quickly and content has a short shelf life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools to produce or tailor content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience facilitating executive discussions, not only preparing others to lead them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Worked with customers in regulated industries such as financial services, healthcare, or the public sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$320,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$400,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;SLSQ427R457&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director, AI Sales (IC)&lt;/strong&gt; to grow Databricks’ enterprise AI business and shape how we take AI to market. You will work directly with executives and technical teams to win strategic opportunities, get AI applications into production, and expand customer usage. You will also turn what works with customers into sales plays the broader field can execute, with direct influence on our AI product priorities and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver assigned AI consumption, bookings, and activation goals by prioritizing high-potential strategic accounts and converting underserved or unactivated demand into production usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase the number of enterprise AI opportunities that achieve executive-backed technical validation and progress from experimentation to repeatable production workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale field plays around priority AI platform capabilities including AI Gateway, AI/ML training and serving infrastructure, Agent Bricks for custom agent development, etc. Creating measurable pipeline and consumption growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve field execution by equipping and enabling account teams and specialists with repeatable guidance on AI use-case discovery, qualification, value articulation, pricing, sizing, and opportunity progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a scalable engagement model across sales, solutions architecture, business-unit enablement, and partners that increases specialist-influenced pipeline and accelerates customer decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn customer, field, and competitive feedback into clear product and go-to-market recommendations that strengthen Databricks’ position in the enterprise AI market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal and external executive credibility for Databricks AI, increasing strategic sponsorship and expanding adoption across priority accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated enterprise sales or consulting experience in AI platforms, AI infrastructure, machine learning, developer platforms, or related technical software, with a track record of delivering growth against measurable goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating go-to-market strategy in an emerging or ambiguous technical market, including the ability to prioritize across a broad, changing account and opportunity landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of enterprise AI architecture and the platform capabilities required to build, deploy, govern, and scale models, agents, and AI applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to earn technical approval and executive sponsorship through workshops, onsite engagements, business cases, and clearly defined validation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating field enablement and repeatable GTM plays that improve how sellers qualify, position, price, size, and advance complex technical opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence internally as well as externally, aligning sales, solutions architecture, business-unit leaders, enablement teams, and partners around a common AI growth strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, credible, and comfortable operating without a predefined account list or fully formed playbook while maintaining disciplined prioritization and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2729&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected base salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipated utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$374,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$374,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$374,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 4 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$374,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&lt;strong&gt; Brokerage Platform&lt;/strong&gt; org is the backbone of everything Robinhood trades, clears, and settles. It is the underlying infrastructure that powers every equities trade, every options contract, every event contract, and every crypto transaction that moves through our platform — and it is the foundation on which Robinhood&#39;s most important business lines are built. The org spans four deeply interconnected teams: Market Data &amp;amp; Symbology (the real-time and reference data layer that the entire product experience depends on), Trading Platform (core order routing, execution management, and bulk order systems), Clearing (settlement, margin, security lending, cash sweep, and the full back-office operations stack), and Brokerage Infrastructure (the platform layer that enables every product team to move faster through abstractions, reliability investments, and next-generation stack modernization). This org operates 24 hours a day around critical market functions — from market open to trade settlement — and when things go wrong, it matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Engineering, Brokerage Platform&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead one of Robinhood&#39;s largest and most consequential engineering organizations. You will own the technical strategy, people leadership, and delivery execution for a broad, high-stakes platform — partnering closely with a dedicated TPM and engaging deeply with trading, crypto, and active trader product teams who depend on your org every day. This is not a role for someone who manages from a distance. You will need the engineering depth to challenge technical bets, the platform mindset to drive the investments that move the business forward, and the leadership presence to build and retain a world-class team in a domain where the stakes are always high.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our &lt;strong&gt;Menlo Park, CA&lt;/strong&gt; office, with in-person attendance expected &lt;strong&gt;5 &lt;/strong&gt;days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full engineering strategy and delivery for Brokerage Platform — spanning Market Data &amp;amp; Symbology, Trading Platform, Clearing, and Brokerage Infrastructure — setting the technical direction and ensuring the org executes with reliability and conviction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a large, distributed engineering organization of senior and staff-level engineers and engineering managers — building the talent, culture, and bench strength the org needs to sustain high performance over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive platform investments that have direct business impact — identifying the modernization, reliability, and scalability bets worth making, building the conviction behind them, and seeing them through to measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner tightly with your TPM counterpart to manage a high volume of incoming asks from trading, crypto, active trader, and event contracts product teams — prioritizing ruthlessly and protecting engineering capacity for the work that matters most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the reliability and operational health of systems that run continuously around market-critical functions — ensuring the org is prepared for high-severity incidents and has the processes and tooling to resolve them fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage deeply with cross-functional leadership across Robinhood — representing Brokerage Platform&#39;s roadmap, dependencies, and capabilities to product, ops, and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion platform modernization and technical debt reduction — driving initiatives like stack rewrites, sharding, multi-region scaling, and infrastructure abstractions that unlock velocity across the entire engineering org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of software engineering experience, with 6+ years in engineering leadership roles — including demonstrated experience as a Director or Senior Director managing large, multi-team engineering organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep platform engineering background — you&#39;ve owned and driven the technical direction of foundational backend platforms at scale, not just product features built on top of them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(big plus, though not directly required) Experience at the intersection of financial services, trading, brokerage, or adjacent high-criticality domains is a strong plus — you don&#39;t need to know all four of our sub-domains, but depth in one or two (market data, clearing, order execution, or brokerage infrastructure) is a meaningful signal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving platform modernization bets that delivered real business outcomes — you&#39;ve made the case for a large technical investment, executed it, and pointed to the result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a high-severity, always-on engineering environment — you&#39;ve led teams through major incidents and built the systems and culture to minimize their recurrence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background with distributed systems, backend services at scale, Go or Python, and cloud infrastructure (AWS preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background from high-performance engineering organizations in fintech, trading, crypto, or large-scale consumer platforms — companies similar to Robinhood, Coinbase, SoFi, Google, or similar environments where the platform was the business is a strong plus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambitious roadmap requires a great culture shaped by exceptional leaders. Here’s what we expect from them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high performance by setting clear, focused goals, giving real-time feedback, stretching top talent, and scaling impact through focus, innovation, and tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and retain top talent by setting a high bar, hiring only those who raise it, investing in onboarding, and addressing talent issues quickly and fairly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create community by connecting work to purpose, removing friction while prioritizing safety, building trust and inclusion, and leading from the front with integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Tier benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the Robinhood Employee Fund that gives eligible US employees the opportunity to invest in a private employee fund that provides exposure to Robinhood Ventures funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$294,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$345,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$294,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$345,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$294,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$345,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Usage Disclosure:&lt;/strong&gt; Robinhood uses artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of our recruiting process. These tools enhance the efficiency and consistency of our hiring process; however, all hiring decisions are made by our hiring teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DESIGN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put your design skills to work at a cutting-edge company that challenges the norm.&amp;nbsp; From character and level design to competitive gameplay and system design, help shape the future of interactive entertainment at Epic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Director of Design focusing on Fortnite, you will be responsible for leading and collaborating with a multidisciplinary team of developers to guide Fortnite modes to success from ideation to ship. Working with senior leadership, you will carry the game&#39;s vision and Epic’s goals forward while making hard calls on quality and priorities, and, above all, be creatively excited and engaged in creating an unforgettable, fun experience for our players.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with senior leadership to define a vision and business goals for a season within Fortnite Battle Royale, Reload, and more shooter modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a design team and hone the design craft for Fortnite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold that&amp;nbsp; design vision across the company with clarity and excitement, and inspire the design team to follow you; uphold Epic’s design and gameplay quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee design and development from start to finish - From leading ideation with the team and shaping a timeline of engagement across the whole season, to making tough decisions on quality and scope throughout production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a design roadmap that drives multiple seasons, along with system roadmaps that underpin those seasons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Managers and Analytics teams to gain insights from player metrics and marketplace data, then translate those insights into actionable goals to improve the player experience; work with Production, discipline leads, and HR to manage staffing, feature scope, production milestones, and hiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a multidisciplinary leadership team - monitoring the culture and performance of the overall Fortnite development organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on mentoring and empowering the design team to be independently successful and make solid decisions without your involvement; foster curiosity and healthy risk-taking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading game teams from a director or other high-level design leadership perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rich background in game systems that operate at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An expert-level background in a creative craft you can speak to and draw from&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of what makes games tick at all levels, with a particular focus on what makes them fun, immersive experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A keen understanding of what makes the Battle Royale genre work is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion and excitement for applying yourself to highly complicated problem spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent soft skills; you are able to navigate the day-to-day ups and downs of working with a large team across many disciplines and locations with ease&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An eye and passion for helping to creatively shape a product that goes beyond the game team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you have a portfolio/reel/website you&#39;d like to share, please hyperlink it to your resume or submit it as an attachment with your application.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;EPIC JOB + EPIC BENEFITS = EPIC LIFE&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&quot;&gt;Our intent is to cover all things that are medically necessary and improve the quality of life. We pay 100% of the premiums for both you and your dependents. Our coverage includes Medical, Dental, a Vision HRA, Long Term Disability, Life Insurance &amp;amp; a 401k with competitive match. We also offer a robust mental well-being program through Modern Health, which provides free therapy and coaching for employees &amp;amp; dependents. Throughout the year we celebrate our employees with events and company-wide paid breaks. We offer unlimited PTO and sick time and recognize individuals for 7 years of employment with a paid sabbatical.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Pay Transparency Information&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected annual base pay range(s) for this position are detailed below. Each base pay range is relevant only for individuals who are residents of or will be expected to work within the specified locale. Compensation varies based on a variety of factors, which include (but aren’t limited to) things such as skills and competencies, qualifications, knowledge, and experience. In addition to base pay, most employees are eligible to participate in Epic’s generous benefit plans and discretionary incentive programs (subject to the terms of those plans or programs).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;California Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$318,499&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$467,132 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Washington Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$289,544&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$424,665 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games​ ​is a leading interactive entertainment company. For over 30 years we&#39;ve been making award-winning games and engine technology that empowers others to make visually stunning games and 3D content that bring environments to life like never before. Epic&#39;s award-winning Unreal Engine technology not only provides game developers the ability to build high-fidelity, interactive experiences for PC, console, mobile, and VR, it is also a tool being embraced by content creators across a variety of industries such as media and entertainment, automotive, and architectural design. As we continue to build our Engine technology and develop remarkable games, we strive to build teams of world-class talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Like what you hear? Come be a part of something Epic!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games deeply values diverse teams and an inclusive work culture, and we are proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer. Learn more about our Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/eeo-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note to Recruitment Agencies: &lt;/strong&gt;Epic does not accept any unsolicited resumes or approaches from any unauthorized third party (including recruitment or placement agencies) (i.e., a third party with whom we do not have a negotiated and validly executed agreement). We will not pay any fees to any unauthorized third party. Further details on these matters can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/note-to-recruitment-agencies&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ART&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Push your artistic talent to the limit on a team of world-class environment, character and concept artists who strive to innovate and inspire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Lead Technical Artist to guide a team of Technical Artists in building visually compelling, performant game worlds as part of our collaboration with Disney. Working closely with Art, Engineering, and Design, you&#39;ll translate project goals into practical tools, workflows, and technical solutions. This is a hands-on leadership role focused on day-to-day execution, team mentorship, and solving production challenges. You&#39;ll help deliver the studio&#39;s technical art direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Profile game content and resolve performance bottlenecks in collaboration with Art and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Optimize geometry, materials, shaders, textures, lighting, foliage, and VFX to meet established performance and memory budgets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Help artists apply best practices for LODS, instancing, streaming, and content scalability across target platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Conduct content reviews and develop validation tools to identify technical issues early&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Develop and maintain tools that support efficient environment creation, including terrain, foliage, procedural generation, and asset placement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Partner with Environment Art and Level Design to improve world-building workflows and troubleshoot production issues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Implement established standards for modular assets, materials, and content organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Document tools and workflows, helping artists adopt them effectively&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Lead the day-to-day work of a small Technical Art team, coordinating priorities and deliverables with Production and technical leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Mentor Technical Artists through feedback, technical reviews, and hands-on problem-solving&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Balance individual contributions with delegation, giving team members clear ownership and opportunities to grow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Communicate progress, dependencies, and technical risks to project leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Coordinate Initiatives with Tech Art Leads on other projects working in the same development environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Help establish practical usage guidelines and train artists on approved workflows, following studio policies for intellectual property, licensing, and data security&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Evaluate results against quality and efficiency goals, recommending which workflows to refine or expand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Experience shipping and supporting a live-service game&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong professional experience in technical art for games, including contributions to a shipped title or comparably complex production&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Experience leading or mentoring Technical Artists and coordinating technical work across disciplines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Practical knowledge of real-time rendering, profiling, content optimization, and performance budgets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Experience with world-building pipelines, procedural workflows, LOD systems, and content streaming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Proficiency with Unreal Engine, Unity, or a proprietary game engine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Scripting or programming experience for tool development, using languages such as Python, C#, or C++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Familiarity with shader and material development, alongside tools such as Houdini, Maya, or Blender&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong problem-solving, communication, and prioritization skills, with an appreciation for artistic quality&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is open to multiple locations across the US (including CA, NYC, &amp;amp; WA). &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Pay Transparency Information&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected annual base pay range(s) for this position are detailed below. Each base pay range is relevant only for individuals who are residents of or will be expected to work within the specified locale. Compensation varies based on a variety of factors, which include (but aren’t limited to) things such as skills and competencies, qualifications, knowledge, and experience. In addition to base pay, most employees are eligible to participate in Epic’s generous benefit plans and discretionary incentive programs (subject to the terms of those plans or programs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;New York City Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$235,042&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$344,728 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;California Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,456&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$316,001 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Washington Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,869&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$287,274 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h2&gt;
